RATIONALE: "RED because the systems contribution is not a design and not a shipping-systems insight beyond known lexical scoring behavior. The packet’s load-bearing L1 result falsifies the broad corpus-hygiene risk framing: realistic dense retrieval is flat, while the survivor is BM25-only. Existing shipping lexical systems already expose the mechanism: Lucene BM25Similarity documents b as controlling document-length normalization and scores tf as freq/(freq+k1*(1-b+b*dl/avgdl)); rank-bm25 implements both BM25Okapi and BM25L with the same b-normalized denominator plus BM25L delta. The packet’s b=0 abolition and BM25L persistence are good mechanistic checks, but they mainly demonstrate consequences of established length normalization under synthetic query-term stuffing. Reproducibility is partial: L0 artifacts are summarized with sanity checks, but L1 raw_results.csv is reported as remote-only on devgpu014, so independent artifact review is incomplete."
